f how fox news is funded in this  way and number two it allows you to tell  your cable provider to separate out fox  news to make it an optional channel on  just about every cable system you can't  say i don't want fox if you don't want  to pay for hbo on every cable system  that i'm aware of you just say i don't  want hbo great you don't get hbo and you  don't pay for hbo on most cable systems  you can't remove fox news and fox  business okay if you pay for for cable  or satellite tv you are subsidizing fox  news whether you watch it or not  the uh  the cable provider pays fox and they  pass the cost directly to you  now we've said before i've explained to  you fox doesn't depend that much on ad  revenue why not  because of these monthly fees from  subscribers when all of those  advertisers bailed on tucker carlson's  show and we watched an episode and we  saw that he had almost no advertisers  left and the advertisers he had left  were sort of like  low rent low low value kind of low brow  advertisers the mic pillows of the world  and stuff like that we laughed about it  and we had a grand old time but we  acknowledged that it doesn't really  matter that much because fox news's  revenue model two-thirds comes from  subscriber fees through cable providers  fox news makes close to two billion  dollars a year  from these hidden subscriber fees that's  twice what cnn makes and it's three  times as much as msnbc makes so sadly  all of our money if we have cable is  being used to fund this extremist  programming you should not be forced to  subsidize fox news but you don't have a  choice if you have a cable subscription  so check out unfox my cable box read  about it  fill it out which will send a message to  your cable provider telling them  separate this out a lot allow me to say  no  and that's what we really have to do i  mean obviously we can also cut the cord  the sad part about cutting the cord  while many people have done it and i  don't have any moral opposition to it  we we recently learned that thanks to  cord cutting  c-span which is a very valuable service  which has no ad revenue c-span has been  significantly hurt by cost cutting so  that's the tragic thing you might say  well i'll cut the cord to stop funding  fox great but then you also end up  hurting c-span which we don't want to  hurt c-span provides a valuable public  service so we have to pressure the cable  and satellite providers to stop  including fox news by default  you should be able to say i don't want  fox and if you don't want fox you  shouldn't have to pay for fox and the  cable provider shouldn't have to pay for  fox regardless that's the sort of system  that needs to be upended we're going to  keep you updated there's currently  negotiations actually happening right  now fox and cable providers are  negotiating their next contracts on this  on these subscriber fees and  we could really kneecap fox news it's  not a limitation on speech anybody who  wants to fund fox should be able to  anybody who wants to watch it should be  able to nobody should be silencing fox  fox can do whatever they want but  we shouldn't by default be paying for  fox news when we certainly don't watch  it and absolutely don't want to be  funding it we'll have more on this on  our instagram which you can find at  david pakman show
 

